{"id":"winsound/MessageBeep","module":"winsound","qualname":"MessageBeep","name":"MessageBeep","kind":"function","parent":null,"signatures":["MessageBeep(type=MB_OK)"],"doc":"Call the underlying MessageBeep() function from the Platform API. This plays a sound as specified in the registry. The type argument specifies which sound to play; possible values are -1, MB_ICONASTERISK, MB_ICONEXCLAMATION, MB_ICONHAND, MB_ICONQUESTION, and MB_OK, all described below. The value -1 produces a “simple beep”; this is the final fallback if a sound cannot be played otherwise. If the system indicates an error, RuntimeError is raised.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/winsound.html#winsound.MessageBeep","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["Windows"],"source":null,"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"winsound/PlaySound","module":"winsound","qualname":"PlaySound","name":"PlaySound","kind":"function","parent":null,"signatures":["PlaySound(sound, flags)"],"doc":"Call the underlying PlaySound() function from the Platform API. The sound parameter may be a filename, a system sound alias, audio data as a bytes-like object, or None. Its interpretation depends on the value of flags, which can be a bitwise ORed combination of the constants described below. If the sound parameter is None, any currently playing waveform sound is stopped. If the system indicates an error, RuntimeError is raised.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/winsound.html#winsound.PlaySound","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["Windows"],"source":null,"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"winsound/SND_ALIAS","module":"winsound","qualname":"SND_ALIAS","name":"SND_ALIAS","kind":"data","parent":null,"signatures":[],"doc":"The sound parameter is a sound association name from the registry. If the registry contains no such name, play the system default sound unless SND_NODEFAULT is also specified. If no default sound is registered, raise RuntimeError. Do not use with SND_FILENAME.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/winsound.html#winsound.SND_ALIAS","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["Windows"],"source":null,"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"winsound/SND_APPLICATION","module":"winsound","qualname":"SND_APPLICATION","name":"SND_APPLICATION","kind":"data","parent":null,"signatures":[],"doc":"The sound parameter is an application-specific alias in the registry. This flag can be combined with the SND_ALIAS flag to specify an application-defined sound alias.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/winsound.html#winsound.SND_APPLICATION","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["Windows"],"source":null,"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"winsound/SND_ASYNC","module":"winsound","qualname":"SND_ASYNC","name":"SND_ASYNC","kind":"data","parent":null,"signatures":[],"doc":"Return immediately, allowing sounds to play asynchronously.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/winsound.html#winsound.SND_ASYNC","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["Windows"],"source":null,"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"winsound/SND_FILENAME","module":"winsound","qualname":"SND_FILENAME","name":"SND_FILENAME","kind":"data","parent":null,"signatures":[],"doc":"The sound parameter is the name of a WAV file. Do not use with SND_ALIAS.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/winsound.html#winsound.SND_FILENAME","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["Windows"],"source":null,"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"winsound/SND_LOOP","module":"winsound","qualname":"SND_LOOP","name":"SND_LOOP","kind":"data","parent":null,"signatures":[],"doc":"Play the sound repeatedly. The SND_ASYNC flag must also be used to avoid blocking. Cannot be used with SND_MEMORY.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/winsound.html#winsound.SND_LOOP","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["Windows"],"source":null,"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"winsound/SND_MEMORY","module":"winsound","qualname":"SND_MEMORY","name":"SND_MEMORY","kind":"data","parent":null,"signatures":[],"doc":"The sound parameter to PlaySound() is a memory image of a WAV file, as a bytes-like object.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/winsound.html#winsound.SND_MEMORY","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["Windows"],"source":null,"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"winsound/SND_NODEFAULT","module":"winsound","qualname":"SND_NODEFAULT","name":"SND_NODEFAULT","kind":"data","parent":null,"signatures":[],"doc":"If the specified sound cannot be found, do not play the system default sound.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/winsound.html#winsound.SND_NODEFAULT","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["Windows"],"source":null,"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"winsound/SND_NOSTOP","module":"winsound","qualname":"SND_NOSTOP","name":"SND_NOSTOP","kind":"data","parent":null,"signatures":[],"doc":"Do not interrupt sounds currently playing.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/winsound.html#winsound.SND_NOSTOP","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["Windows"],"source":null,"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
